00:14:34.370 --> 00:14:35.500
Then can I use it?

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.080
Okay, okay.

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.080
Here.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:40.750
You have nothing else to wear, right?

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:43.660
You can wash your own clothes, though.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:47.910
"I ♥ Space"

00:14:47.910 --> 00:14:50.410
"I ♥ Space"
Tacky.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:00.950
--R-Robby!
--Wha--?!

00:15:00.950 --> 00:15:02.950
Hey, you! I told you not to come over here!

00:15:02.950 --> 00:15:04.080
Ooh, you looked at my face.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:06.160
Ooh, you spoke to me.

00:15:09.620 --> 00:15:11.000
Ah, what's the use?

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:15.040
For now, about all we can do
is keep heading for Isekandar.

00:15:18.750 --> 00:15:20.290
Oh, it looks good on you.

00:15:20.290 --> 00:15:23.500
How do you figure?! What kind
of lame pajamas are these?

00:15:23.500 --> 00:15:25.080
Where do they sell them?

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:28.660
If you wanna borrow them,
don't complain. If not, go naked.

00:15:28.660 --> 00:15:31.500
I don't want <i>that</i>. I guess
I'll put up with these for now,

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:33.950
and buy another set at
some world along the way.

00:15:35.040 --> 00:15:40.330
You know, come to think of it, for all
the mail-order shopping he did,

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:44.120
he never did buy pajamas,
and always wore those.

00:15:53.410 --> 00:15:57.000
Man, what are you doing in here,
with the lights so low?

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.580
Leave me alone.

00:15:58.580 --> 00:16:01.250
If you like candles so much, here.

00:16:03.450 --> 00:16:04.580
Huh?

00:16:04.580 --> 00:16:08.000
I got it from the travel bureau chief
on Mars when we left.

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:12.910
I don't use them myself, so you can have it.
Just don't start any fires.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:27.450
Sightseeing on Pinopendio was fun.

00:16:27.450 --> 00:16:31.750
The Ossu! Yasujiro Seishunkan
Museum was the best!

00:16:31.750 --> 00:16:33.870
This photo turned out well, too.

00:16:33.870 --> 00:16:36.620
Well, I think the real thing
might be even better.

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:38.750
--Leave it to you, Mr. Yang!
--Leave it to you, Mr. Yang!

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:42.370
The Pinopendio Cotton Weaving
Center was also great.

00:16:42.370 --> 00:16:45.540
Mr. Yang, you were great at the
loom-your-own-fabric exhibit!

00:16:45.540 --> 00:16:49.540
Your high-speed weaving technique
had the whole gallery stunned!

00:16:50.790 --> 00:16:52.700
Heh, it was no big deal.

00:16:52.700 --> 00:16:54.620
--That's our Mr. Yang!
--That's our Mr. Yang!

00:16:54.620 --> 00:16:59.370
All that remains is to wait for <i>him</i>
to be escorted from the checkpoint.

00:16:59.370 --> 00:17:03.080
Come on, Robby!

00:17:03.080 --> 00:17:06.160
Okay, we're at the warp point. Here we go!

00:17:17.660 --> 00:17:19.700
That was quite a jolt, huh?

00:17:23.120 --> 00:17:24.700
--Wh-What the hell is this?!
--Whoa, hold on a minute!

00:17:24.700 --> 00:17:27.660
--Hey, we're back on the hyperroad--
--Wh-What the hell is this?!
--Whoa, hold on a minute!

00:17:27.660 --> 00:17:29.450
What the hell are you doing?!

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:31.200
Are you trying to burn down the spaceship?!

00:17:31.200 --> 00:17:32.450
Don't look at me!

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:34.870
Why aren't the sprinklers kicking in?!

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:39.790
Huh? Oh, I didn't want to get soaked again,
so I closed the main valve.

00:17:39.790 --> 00:17:41.290
--You idiot!
--You idiot!

00:17:41.290 --> 00:17:42.450
Damn it.

00:17:43.660 --> 00:17:45.040
Come on, come on...

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:45.750
Stop!

00:17:45.750 --> 00:17:46.540
Huh?

00:17:46.540 --> 00:17:49.250
Those are my favorite pajamas!

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:50.620
Huh...?

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:53.000
Ikku Fireman Mode!

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:03.080
Mission complete.

00:18:10.830 --> 00:18:11.830
Here.

00:18:12.910 --> 00:18:17.160
After this, you can wear these lame
pajamas for the rest of your life.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:25.410
I think I'll take you up on that.

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:30.080
For crying out loud, you and I
really took a detour there, huh?

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.120
That's because you were nagging me so much.

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.200
Yeah, yeah.

00:18:33.200 --> 00:18:35.580
Just be sure to start putting
the toilet seat down next time.

00:18:35.580 --> 00:18:38.450
As long as you cut back on the toilet paper.

00:18:38.450 --> 00:18:42.580
Looks like that storm has cleared the air.
And now, a quick verse.

00:18:42.580 --> 00:18:48.290
"Burning down walls deepens the bonds
of friendship along this journey." By Ikku.

00:18:51.450 --> 00:18:53.580
Hey, about where are we now?

00:18:53.580 --> 00:18:57.200
Once we warp out, we'll be at the
last checkpoint before Isekandar.

00:18:57.200 --> 00:18:58.000
'Kay.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.120
No, it's not "'kay"! What are you gonna do?!

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.160
We can't go any farther like this!

00:19:02.160 --> 00:19:04.540
I don't know what you want me to tell you.

00:19:04.540 --> 00:19:06.910
I can't take my name off the blacklist.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.620
Be that as it may...

00:19:08.620 --> 00:19:12.950
Listen, Hatchi, if it comes to it,
you go on by yourself.

00:19:14.290 --> 00:19:15.870
Is he in the bathroom?

00:19:18.410 --> 00:19:20.200
"Robby Yarge"

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:36.080
Or we could just blow through the checkpoint.

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:38.750
We might actually slip our
way through, you know.

00:19:38.750 --> 00:19:40.500
No, not a chance.

00:19:40.500 --> 00:19:42.290
Nope, maybe we will.

00:19:43.450 --> 00:19:46.250
You were in there a while.

00:19:46.250 --> 00:19:51.950
You know, I've never had so many
unexpected events, one after another.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:57.540
So maybe they might keep on happening--
unexpected events.

00:19:57.540 --> 00:19:59.830
We've already come all this way.

00:19:59.830 --> 00:20:03.370
We have nothing to lose,
so let's press on and go for broke.

00:20:04.410 --> 00:20:07.450
There's something... different about you.

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:10.290
There is? If so, whose fault is that?

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:12.830
Yeah, whose fault indeed?

00:20:12.830 --> 00:20:15.200
What the hell, let's do it!

00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.450
Coming out of warp!

00:20:16.450 --> 00:20:17.790
--All right!
--Mm-hmm!

00:20:21.410 --> 00:20:24.790
Ooh, so this is the last checkpoint.

00:20:24.790 --> 00:20:27.660
Let's head on in like nothing's wrong.

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:34.040
Please transmit your passport code.

00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:39.330
Hmm, and if this gets kicked back to us,
we break through like we're hoping to.

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:41.250
That's conceivable.

00:20:43.290 --> 00:20:46.040
Confirmed. Passage approved.

00:20:46.040 --> 00:20:47.370
Huh?

00:20:47.370 --> 00:20:48.500
We're through!

00:20:48.500 --> 00:20:50.160
That's unexpected!

00:20:50.160 --> 00:20:52.910
How can we pass through with Robby in here?

00:20:52.910 --> 00:20:54.700
Did they not check very hard?

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.540
Everything turned out all right.

00:20:56.540 --> 00:20:57.830
Yeah, yeah!

00:20:57.830 --> 00:21:02.120
We're about to arrive at Isekandar!
We're finally here, Hatchi!

00:21:02.120 --> 00:21:03.450
Yep.

00:21:05.160 --> 00:21:06.200
Yes!

00:21:06.200 --> 00:21:11.540
Let's get our hands on some Akafucrystals,
and find happiness!

00:21:13.750 --> 00:21:17.330
Impounding these spaceships we busted!

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:21.410
Come on! Get walking!

00:21:21.410 --> 00:21:23.450
--Wow...
--Wow...

00:21:23.450 --> 00:21:26.620
There sure are a lot of
people on the blacklist, huh?

00:21:26.620 --> 00:21:29.330
They all look pretty stupid now.

00:21:29.330 --> 00:21:33.950
Heh, and Robby should be getting
perp-walked by here any moment.

00:21:40.660 --> 00:21:42.910
We've tracked his current location.

00:21:42.910 --> 00:21:47.910
According to his Smartbracelet credit history,
he appears to be heading for Isekandar.

00:21:47.910 --> 00:21:52.660
Very well. The Luna Guard are
now heading to Isekandar.

00:21:52.660 --> 00:21:54.200
Full speed ahead!

00:22:00.080 --> 00:22:01.250
Look!

00:22:01.250 --> 00:22:03.080
That's Isekandar!

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:07.330
That's awesome! It's shining like crazy!

00:22:07.330 --> 00:22:10.500
It doesn't look all that tasteful, does it?

00:22:10.500 --> 00:22:13.750
Don't say that about the
miracle world of Isekandar!

00:22:13.750 --> 00:22:14.910
You're right.

00:22:14.910 --> 00:22:18.540
Okay, let's go! To the world of happiness!

00:23:51.910 --> 00:23:53.040
"Next time"
"#11 'Common Fame Is a Common Isekandar'"

00:23:53.040 --> 00:23:56.910
"Next time"
"#11 'Common Fame Is a Common Isekandar'"
Next time, "Common Fame Is a Common Isekandar."

00:23:57.160 --> 00:24:01.870
"After the long wait, they've finally arrived!"
"The far end of space, Isekandar"

00:24:02.040 --> 00:24:06.950
"Will Robby be able to find
the fortune-bringing Akafucrystals?"
